{"id":9180,"date":"2021-07-29T00:00:00","date_gmt":"2021-07-29T06:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rethinkfirst.com\/resources\/teaching-safety-skills-to-individuals-with-autism-webinar\/"},"modified":"2025-02-27T17:45:09","modified_gmt":"2025-02-27T22:45:09","slug":"teaching-safety-skills-to-individuals-with-autism-webinar","status":"publish","type":"resources","link":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/teaching-safety-skills-to-individuals-with-autism-webinar\/","title":{"rendered":"Teaching Safety Skills to Individuals with Autism"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"9180\" class=\"elementor elementor-9180\" data-elementor-post-type=\"resources\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-108cf9e9 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"108cf9e9\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-56c42d3e\" data-id=\"56c42d3e\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5ffd5cb elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"5ffd5cb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"videoDivHolder\"> <div> <video controls poster=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/10\/485-MTE0ODg2OQ_teaching-safety-skills-to-individuals-autism_thumbnail.jpg\"> <source src=\"https:\/\/rtaprodmarketing.blob.core.windows.net\/rta-prod-marketingvideos\/485-MTE0ODg2OQ_teaching-safety-skills-to-individuals-autism.mp4\" type=\"video\/mp4\"> <\/video> <\/div> <\/div> <style> #videoDivHolder { width: 100%; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; } #videoDivHolder > div { position: relative; overflow: hidden; width: 100%; padding-top: 56.25%; } #videoDivHolder > div video { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; bottom: 0; right: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; } <\/style>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>Individuals with autism present with unique challenges that make them at risk for a wide range of safety concerns. They may, for example, wander from caregivers, be unable to seek assistance when lost and may not know how to respond to unwanted advances by strangers in the community. There have been a number of studies documenting a functional analysis of some unsafe behaviors such as elopement. This has led to the development of function-based treatments and strategies that can potentially prevent unsafe behavior.<\/p>\n<p>This presentation will review recent research in the area of safety assessment and interventions and provide proactive, practical strategies and resources, to help ensure the safety of individuals with autism.<\/p>\n<h2>Takeaways<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify why individuals with autism are at a risk for safety concerns.<\/li>\n<li>Identify current applied research directives to address safety concerns.<\/li>\n<li>Identify components of functional analysis of elopement.<\/li>\n<li>Identify skills to teach to address safety skills of individuals with autism.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>There is no cost to attend and this webinar is not eligible for CEUs. The presentation will be posted on our blog within two weeks.<\/p>\n<h2>About the Guest Speaker<\/h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-b4ad576 authorSection elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"b4ad576\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-8762fab\" data-id=\"8762fab\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e958cdb elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"e958cdb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"280\" height=\"280\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/04\/bridget-taylor-rethink.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-11281\" alt=\"Bridget A. Taylor Headshot\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/04\/bridget-taylor-rethink.jpg 280w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/04\/bridget-taylor-rethink-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 280px) 100vw, 280px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-66 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-2c10ba8\" data-id=\"2c10ba8\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ee71265 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ee71265\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Dr. Bridget Taylor, PsyD, BCBA-D<\/h3><p><span style=\"color: #333333;\">Executive Director of Alpine Learning Group\/ Senior Clinical Advisor for Rethink<\/span><\/p><p>Dr. Bridget A. Taylor is co-founder and CEO of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.alpinelearninggroup.org\/about-us\/staff\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alpine Learning Group<\/a> and is Senior Clinical Advisor for <a href=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkfirst.com\/team-experts\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rethink<\/a>. Dr. Taylor has specialized in the education of children with Autism for over 30 years. She holds a Doctor of Psychology from Rutgers University and received her Master\u2019s degree in Early Childhood Special Education from Columbia University. She is a Board-Certified Behavior Analyst and a Licensed Psychologist. She is past president of the Behavior Analyst Certification Board and past Associate Editor of the <a href=\"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/journal\/19383703\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Journal of Applied Behavior Analysis<\/a>. She currently serves on several editorial boards and the Autism Advisory Group for the Cambridge Center for Behavioral Studies.<\/p><p>Active in the Autism research community, Dr. Taylor has published numerous peer-reviewed research articles and book chapters, on innovative practices to improve the lives of individuals with autism. Dr. Taylor was recently recognized by the Association for Applied Behavior Analysis International for her outstanding contributions and was given <a href=\"https:\/\/www1.abainternational.org\/constituents\/bios\/bridgettaylor.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ABAI\u2019s Fellow designation<\/a>.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":15007,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Webinar: Teaching Safety Skills to Individuals with Autism","_seopress_titles_desc":"Ensure safety of individuals with autism with recent research of safety assessment & interventions & provide proactive, practical strategies & resources.","_seopress_robots_index":"","om_disable_all_campaigns":false,"_links_to":"","_links_to_target":""},"audience":[70],"resource-type":[72],"resource-topic":[328,97,329,93,230],"resource-tag":[336,268,308,324,374,156],"class_list":["post-9180","resources","type-resources","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","audience-providers","resource-type-webinar","resource-topic-assessment","resource-topic-autism","resource-topic-behavior","resource-topic-community","resource-topic-research","resource-tag-asd","resource-tag-caregiver","resource-tag-health-plans","resource-tag-member-engagement","resource-tag-safety","resource-tag-teacher"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/9180","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/resources"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/19"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/9180\/revisions"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/15007"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=9180"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"audience","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/audience?post=9180"},{"taxonomy":"resource-type","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-type?post=9180"},{"taxonomy":"resource-topic","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-topic?post=9180"},{"taxonomy":"resource-tag","embeddable":true,"hr